From 4041fd8a386243448013897bc44ecafbe7eceac8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:27:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(validator): judge the 2025-11-25 ping, progress and
 cancellation clauses

Eleven checks in a new `checks::basic_utilities` module, each reading both
directions because either party issues requests at this revision: a server's
`roots/list` may opt into progress and may be cancelled by the server that sent
it. That is why these are not the `stateless::progress`/`cancellation` checks,
which read one direction, and why nothing there is reused or changed.

- `ping.empty-result`: an answered ping's result is empty (`_meta` allowed);
  "promptly" is time and is not judged.
- `progress.token-string-or-integer`, `.token-unique-among-active-requests`
  (per party, until the answer), `.value-strictly-increases` (restarting when a
  new request takes the token up).
- `progress.token-issued-in-session`: a token no request of the addressed party
  provided, judged only when the recording holds the session's `initialize`;
  without it the capture may have begun mid-session and nothing is judged.
- `progress.stops-after-completion`: stdio only, where the channel's order is
  the sender's; a task-augmented request answered with a `CreateTaskResult`
  finishes when the task reaches a terminal status (`tasks/get`, `tasks/cancel`,
  `tasks/result`, `notifications/tasks/status`), not at the answer.
- `progress.task-token-unchanged`: progress tied to a task by
  `io.modelcontextprotocol/related-task` keeps the task request's token.
- `cancellation.references-issued-request`: the named id was issued in the
  same direction, with the same `initialize` witness; the "believed in-progress"
  half is the sender's belief and the race the page names, and is not judged.
- `cancellation.initialize-not-cancelled`, `cancellation.task-cancelled-by-request`
  (a request answered with a task is cancelled with `tasks/cancel`).
- `cancellation.no-response-after-cancellation`: an answer to a cancelled request
  only once the receiver demonstrably read the cancellation (it answered a
  request sent after it), stdio only, both directions; the race is not convicted.

Every check counts its subjects after its scope filters, so a session with no
ping, progress or cancellation traffic reports the clauses not observed, and a
2026-07-28-shaped session (no handshake) is not convicted of anything its
recording cannot show. 29 unit tests; each check was hand-mutated twice (a
flipped comparison, a widened match) and each mutant turned a test red.

